> > sound files Dag uploaded, exactly?
> >
> > Let me extract the place info from jbofihe and I'll give Dag a
> > list of the place stuff.
>
> I have the jbofihe data.  It has everything we need to automatically
> generate short versions of all the gismu places, and IMO all the
> stuff we need for the full gismu stuff as well.
>

Robin, have you even looked at the Google doc to which I consistently refer?
All that has already been done. Column 'J' of page 'items' of document
tinyurl.com/smartfmgismu has the jbofi'e phrases for all of the sumti-fied
gismu, and the official definition from the gismu list for the plain gismu.
What's needed is for {lo prenu} to go through the list and make the
definitions, for lack of a better phrase, more humanly understandable.

>
> http://packages.debian.org/source/squeeze/jbofihe -- the relevant
> files are extradict places.dat patterns, and "man smujajgau"
> explains the format, if you have it installed.
>
> I'll see about coming up with complete data files shortly.
>
> -Robin
